From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:07:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: KUnit tests for the driver fixes

Unit tests for the logic of fixes that can run without hardware. They
call the real driver functions on zeroed fake devices; register access
and DMA queue cleanup go to stubs that record what happened.

  mt76-core        radar detection after a sw scan (0011), wcid
                   allocation ranges
  mt76-agg-rx      reorder release exactly at the timeout (0006)
  mt76-connac-mac  fixed-rate TXS keeps the station rate (0005), token
                   put clears the WED count (0007)
  mt7915-mac       zero TWT wake interval (0013), TWT reset (0012), CCA
                   register on mt7916/mt798x (0015), short and truncated
                   tx-free events (0016), tx unblocked after the reset
                   token reclaim (0007)
  mt7915-mcu       firmware reply length checks (0018)

Each test file is included at the end of the source file it tests, so
static functions are reachable, and only when CONFIG_MT76_KUNIT_TEST is
defined. Only a KUnit test build defines it; the image's
modules don't contain the tests. The tx-free tests trigger the
WARN_ON_ONCE() checks they exercise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
